1. LICENSE RATE
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

W5D TECH is licensed at 610.5 TND per hour of work.

Promotional offer valid before 2027 — strictly before 31 December 2026.
After that date, the standard rate applies.

The rate applies to:
  - Initial implementation and onboarding of a new deployment.
  - Custom blocks or modules built for a specific deployment.
  - Migrations, refactors, and feature additions requested by the licensee.
  - Integration work: payment gateways, SMS gateways, OAuth providers,
    external APIs.
  - Training, documentation, and support hours beyond the documented
    baseline.
  - Data migration or schema changes caused by a change of database
    driver (SQLite <-> MySQL/PostgreSQL).
  - Any extension of the progressive pricing curve beyond the canonical
    defaults (see §3).

A running total of hours x 610.5 TND must be visible on the owner
dashboard and in the license footer of every rendered page:

  "W5D Admin Dashboard licensed at 610.5 TND/hour of work.
   Promotional offer valid before 2027."

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
2. OPERATING DOCTRINE — 5% SAMPLING RULE
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

The software enforces a 5% sampling rule on weekly reports:

  - Every week, 5% of submitted reports are randomly selected for
    re-review by the service leader or a delegate.
  - Selection is deterministic per (country_id, week_id) so the sample
    is reproducible.
  - Each sampled report is re-scored against the same rubric the
    manager used, and the result is recorded.
  - A sampled failure triggers the same rework path as a manager
    rejection.

The 5% rate is a fixed operating doctrine of this software. It is not
configurable from the owner dashboard, not editable in configuration
files, and not subject to per-country override. Any fork that changes
this rate must remove the W5D name and branding.

The 5% rate is published on the public status page (/status/) and on
each service page as part of the declared limits.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
3. PROGRESSIVE PRICING — MONEY x TIME
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

The price of a part is NOT FIXED. It is a published function of two
factors:

  p = experts_current / experts_target        (progress, 0 -> 1)
  t = 1 - (deadline - now) / (deadline - start)   (time pressure, 0 -> 1)

The function is:

  price_per_day(p, t)  = base_day  * (1 + alpha * p^p_prog)
                                    * (1 + beta  * t^p_time)
  price_per_week(p, t) = base_week * (1 + alpha * p^p_prog)
                                    * (1 + beta  * t^p_time)

Canonical defaults live in config/variables.php:

  base_day   = 10 TND
  base_week  = 70 TND
  alpha      = 1.0
  beta       = 1.0
  p_prog     = 2.0
  p_time     = 2.0
  cap        = 3.0  (the price can never exceed 3x base)

The following properties are guaranteed by the license:

  - At p = 0 and t = 0, the day price is exactly 10.00 TND and the
    week price is exactly 70.00 TND.
  - At p = 1 and t = 1, the day price is exactly 30.00 TND and the
    week price is exactly 210.00 TND (capped at 3x base).
  - The function is monotonic in both p and t.
  - The function is published on /pricing/ and /investors/ as a live
    chart before any checkout is made.
  - No block may compute a price independently of Pricing.php.
  - Every change to alpha, beta, p_prog, p_time, or cap is written to
    config/variables.php as a dated commit AND to the append-only
    pricing_audit table.

The progressive price is a DECLARED curve, not a scarcity trick. It is
shown alongside the declared limit: "a part is an investment in a path,
not a job."

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
4. HONESTY CONSTRAINT
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

The figure "130,000 experts" is a DESIGN EQUATION:

  5 macro works x 26 services per macro work x 1,000 experts per
  service = 130,000.

It is NOT a claim that 130,000 experts are currently employed by W5D.
As of the date of this license:

  - The real footprint of W5D is 26 developers in Tunisia.
  - The number of certified W5D expert team members is 0.
  - "Live" in the status register does not mean "1,000 experts
    employed".

The software must not be deployed, marketed, or represented in a way
that contradicts this constraint. Every page that mentions the number
130,000 must link to the trust statement (/trust/statement/) and must
not promise a job. The linter enforces this constraint: any hard-coded
"130,000" or "2027" outside config/variables.php and
data/countries/tn.json fails the build.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
5. THE ORIGINAL FRONT-END TEMPLATE
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

The single canonical front-end template shipped with this software is
the `w5d` template, imported from:

  https://github.com/Kaddoussi/w5d

It is the owner's original work: 3 home variants, 14 inner pages, a
Blocks library of 30+ sections, a Heroes library of 12 variants, a
Sections library of 28 sections, a mega-menu, a shell renderer, a
theme system, wired forms, and an animation library.

The template is converted once, during onboarding, into PHP blocks and
components. No content is restated. Tailwind is compiled locally,
Lucide is vendored locally, and fonts are self-hosted. No CDN is used
at runtime.

The license grants the licensee the right to use the `w5d` template as
part of W5D TECH but does NOT grant the right to redistribute the
template as a standalone product or under a different name.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
6. WHAT IS LICENSED
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

The license grants the licensee the right to:

  - Deploy W5D TECH on domains operated by the licensee.
  - Customise the `w5d` template and its blocks for the licensee's own
    deployments.
  - Extend the software with the licensee's own code, provided the
    extensions are not resold as W5D TECH.
  - Run multiple instances (development, staging, production) without
    additional license fees.
  - Choose any supported database driver (SQLite, MySQL, PostgreSQL)
    by setting DB_DRIVER in the .env file. SQLite is the default and
    is the only driver supported on the documented 100 MB VPS budget.
  - Tune the progressive pricing constants (alpha, beta, p_prog,
    p_time, cap) provided every change is committed and logged in
    pricing_audit.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
7. STORAGE BUDGET — LICENSEE RESPONSIBILITY
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

The reference deployment has 100 MB of disk and no MySQL. The README
documents this budget. The licensee is solely responsible for:

  - Configuring STORAGE_DRIVER, ARCHIVE_DRIVER, and BACKUP_DRIVER
    before launch.
  - Ensuring that bin/archive.php, bin/rollup.php, bin/health.php, and
    bin/backup.php run on schedule.
  - Ensuring that the live SQLite database does not exceed the
    documented budget.
  - Switching to an external database provider via DB_DRIVER if the
    VPS budget is exceeded.
  - Any data loss caused by leaving raw weekly_reports in the live
    database beyond the documented window, by disabling the archive
    cron, or by running without a backup.

At full operational scale (130,000 weekly reports per week for a year),
the raw history exceeds the 100 MB budget by roughly an order of
magnitude. The licensee must configure an external archive or an
external database provider for a full-scale deployment.

