────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
9. THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

W5D TECH is delivered with no third-party runtime dependencies:

  - No Composer packages.
  - No CDN requests.
  - No jQuery.
  - No icon font (Lucide is vendored locally as a file).
  - No Tailwind at runtime (compiled to a local CSS file).
  - Fonts are self-hosted (Space Grotesk, Inter).

SQLite is bundled with PHP and is not a third-party dependency. Any
future addition of a third-party dependency must be documented in
docs/dependencies.md with the license of the dependency, its version,
and its URL.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
10. DATA & PRIVACY
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

W5D TECH stores personal data (names, CINs, diplomas, contact
details) for applicants and team members. The licensee is the data
controller for their own deployment and is responsible for compliance
with:

  - Tunisia: Organic Law 2004-63 on personal data protection
    (regulator: INPDP).
  - Any other jurisdiction where the licensee operates.

The software provides consent capture, retention configuration, and
data-subject-request workflows. The licensee must configure these
before launch and must not disable the audit log.

Because SQLite stores all personal data in a single file, the licensee
is responsible for securing that file at the filesystem level (mode
0600, owned by the web user) and for ensuring that any backup of it
is encrypted and stored off-server.

